# Polaris-only UI

Build every screen with Shopify Polaris web components (`s-*`). They carry the Shopify admin theme. Do not create a new UI component, custom control, or visual style.

## Use

- Existing Polaris web components: `s-page`, `s-section`, `s-stack`, `s-grid`, `s-button`, `s-text`, `s-text-field`, `s-banner`, `s-badge`, `s-table`, and the other `s-*` elements in App Home.
- Polaris patterns when the screen matches one: empty state, index table, settings, details, homepage.
- App Bridge for admin chrome: `shopify.toast.show`, `shopify.loading`, `s-app-nav`, and `data-save-bar` on a native `<form>`.
- Global `s-*` tags with no import. Use `@shopify/polaris-types` only when a file needs types.

## Do not

- Do not add a new component, wrapper, or design-system primitive.
- Do not import `@shopify/polaris`, `@shopify/polaris-react`, or `@shopify/polaris-web-components`.
- Do not restyle Polaris with custom CSS, inline styles, or a second theme.
- Do not replace a Polaris component with a styled `div`, `span`, or `button`.
- There is no `s-card` and no `s-form`. Use `s-section` for sections and a native `<form data-save-bar>` for save bars.

```tsx
<s-page heading="Products">
  <s-section heading="All products">
    <s-button variant="primary">Save</s-button>
  </s-section>
</s-page>
```

```tsx
<div className="card">
  <button className="btn-primary">Save</button>
</div>
```

If no Polaris component covers the case, compose existing `s-*` components. Ask before adding anything outside Polaris.
